url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kubeflow/hub/commit/c377bb0649c854af22e4efa853b638bdc5b34b4b","node_id":"C_kwDOLEOEldoAKGMzNzdiYjA2NDljODU0YWYyMmU0ZWZhODUzYjYzOGJkYzViMzRiNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kubeflow/hub/commit/e7bcf4169924cfeef06ed671f7b3193fe248af60","sha":"e7bcf4169924cfeef06ed671f7b3193fe248af60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/commits/e7bcf4169924cfeef06ed671f7b3193fe248af60"}],"sha":"c377bb0649c854af22e4efa853b638bdc5b34b4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/commits/c377bb0649c854af22e4efa853b638bdc5b34b4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9499094?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkuc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkuc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkuc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkuc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkuc","id":9499094,"login":"dkuc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0OTkwOTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkuc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkuc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/commits/e7bcf4169924cfeef06ed671f7b3193fe248af60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:03:00Z","email":"dkuc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dan Kuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:03:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add storage to MCP runtimeMetadata (catalog server + BFF DTO) (#3238)\n\n* Add storage to MCP runtimeMetadata (catalog server + BFF DTO)\n\nMCP servers with a read-only root filesystem need writable paths (e.g. /tmp,\n/app/logs) but the catalog had no way to declare them, so operators had to\npatch each MCPServer by hand after deployment. The catalog server also silently\ndropped any unknown runtimeMetadata field, so the value never reached consumers.\n\nAdd a `storage` array to the MCPRuntimeMetadata OpenAPI schema (v1 + non-v1),\nregenerate the catalog Go model (new MCPStorageMount/MCPStorageSource types),\nand mirror the field in the UI BFF catalog DTO (McpRuntimeMetadata.Storage with\nMcpStorageMount/McpStorageSource). runtimeMetadata is persisted as a single JSON\nblob, so the field round-trips with no DB migration.\n\nConsumers (e.g. the RHOAI MCPServer converter) can map these mounts onto\nspec.config.storage so writable scratch space is provisioned automatically while\nthe root filesystem stays read-only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Dan Kuc <dkuc@redhat.com>\n\n* fix(ui): align MCP storage DTO with catalog contract\n\nAssisted-by: Codex\nSigned-off-by: Dan Kuc <dkuc@redhat.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Dan Kuc <dkuc@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d95a8a7eae4162dfc96d5600179adccdc7f64c76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/git/trees/d95a8a7eae4162dfc96d5600179adccdc7f64c76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/git/commits/e7bcf4169924cfeef06ed671f7b3193fe248af60","verification":{"payload":"tree d95a8a7eae4162dfc96d5600179adccdc7f64c76\nparent 17f8ddbeb7eb8b4ca01f2418e74eea1599818f1e\nauthor Dan Kuc <dkuc@users.noreply.github.com> 1790258580 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790258580 +0000\n\nAdd storage to MCP runtimeMetadata (catalog server + BFF DTO) (#3238)\n\n* Add storage to MCP runtimeMetadata (catalog server + BFF DTO)\n\nMCP servers with a read-only root filesystem need writable paths (e.g. /tmp,\n/app/logs) but the catalog had no way to declare them, so operators had to\npatch each MCPServer by hand after deployment. The catalog server also silently\ndropped any unknown runtimeMetadata field, so the value never reached consumers.\n\nAdd a `storage` array to the MCPRuntimeMetadata OpenAPI schema (v1 + non-v1),\nregenerate the catalog Go model (new MCPStorageMount/MCPStorageSource types),\nand mirror the field in the UI BFF catalog DTO (McpRuntimeMetadata.Storage with\nMcpStorageMount/McpStorageSource). runtimeMetadata is persisted as a single JSON\nblob, so the field round-trips with no DB migration.\n\nConsumers (e.g. the RHOAI MCPServer converter) can map these mounts onto\nspec.config.storage so writable scratch space is provisioned automatically while\nthe root filesystem stays read-only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Dan Kuc <dkuc@redhat.com>\n\n* fix(ui): align MCP storage DTO with catalog contract\n\nAssisted-by: Codex\nSigned-off-by: Dan Kuc <dkuc@redhat.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Dan Kuc <dkuc@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"---