f81a2e49e4c5593c0c548b713d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186957976?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DsThakurRawat","id":186957976,"login":"DsThakurRawat","node_id":"U_kgDOCyTAmA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/commits/9c8ac43ed1596a713d2ea644acae44acb6029e53/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:26:55Z","email":"divyanshrawatofficial@gmail.com","name":"Divyansh Rawat"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:26:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: reject an orderBy the v1 spec does not declare with 400 (#3222)\n\nKEP-0004 requires the v1 APIs to answer 400 when asked to sort on an\nunsupported field. Both servers still fell back to the default column:\nthe generated routers cast the query string without checking it, the\nservices passed it through, and the pagination scope substituted the\ndefault for anything outside its column map.\n\nRegistry v1: buildListOption rejects a value outside the OrderByField\nenum. Catalog v1: a shared validator checks each list endpoint against\nwhat its spec declares. Models accept the enum, ACCURACY (which the\nprovider maps to artifacts.overall_average.double_value),\n<property>.<value_column> and artifacts.<property>.<value_column>. MCP\nservers and tools, agents and skills accept the shared enum. The\nartifact listings keep their documented fallback, and the alpha APIs\nkeep theirs for the deprecation window.\n\nThe catalog Python client docstring no longer lists ACCURACY beside the\nenum values without saying it is a model-only alias.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code\n\nSigned-off-by: Divyansh Rawat <divyanshrawatofficial@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"b0380f703a3c35c70cbd304378b2a26acf915938","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/git/trees/b0380f703a3c35c70cbd304378b2a26acf915938"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/git/commits/9c8ac43ed1596a713d2ea644acae44acb6029e53","verification":{"payload":"tree b0380f703a3c35c70cbd304378b2a26acf915938\nparent 509cfc7229ffee39cd1631329bdeb1e5760e710a\nauthor Divyansh Rawat <divyanshrawatofficial@gmail.com> 1790101615 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790101615 +0000\n\nfix: reject an orderBy the v1 spec does not declare with 400 (#3222)\n\nKEP-0004 requires the v1 APIs to answer 400 when asked to sort on an\nunsupported field. Both servers still fell back to the default column:\nthe generated routers cast the query string without checking it, the\nservices passed it through, and the pagination scope substituted the\ndefault for anything outside its column map.\n\nRegistry v1: buildListOption rejects a value outside the OrderByField\nenum. Catalog v1: a shared validator checks each list endpoint against\nwhat its spec declares. Models accept the enum, ACCURACY (which the\nprovider maps to artifacts.overall_average.double_value),\n<property>.<value_column> and artifacts.<property>.<value_column>. MCP\nservers and tools, agents and skills accept the shared enum. The\nartifact listings keep their documented fallback, and the alpha APIs\nkeep theirs for the deprecation window.\n\nThe catalog Python client docstring no longer lists ACCURACY beside the\nenum values without saying it is a model-only alias.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code\n\nSigned-off-by: Divyansh Rawat <divyanshrawatofficial@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsshvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWTsQAD9hcuTAX1t4SAaia+nQBs8I\nq1X+9wLbN+mD6sQe6Yib2flcKmwVmfR/ieN4iGnokXtbrPsqi20x10pqTiXRGFNR\nqcEcDkfAzLyQCYyDreK/AV+C1/TP3RII6P9lfohYoYxR8Turqpxvcez1CXh8/aX5\nP3V6nYgCdbKAlEBXr/jcK4yI0PcYCdluakuvB3qDSBNBDmEgu+ecnmLLLKAWPGxD\nLd1txoR+YRUd0CkLKMSJd9WylYaXHc3ejXo95Os/HvCR+FOrRiDJZC8KGbeCx0RB\nqnzBhnbHFGYf6sLqgMgFfdKjy/9JFB6cLnKkWJv1ffaEhnZ3bIKrdVtr6aUpyx0z\ndVq73ziYi2ve3pKhX7x3wEEwraIAy5XHZT9JfhKBqSURfi9xV6OXd+1pnFj+So4K\nmdU9Xcu5oglWY5eIGFvi+NAPAZPSwdEFe+VOyWl/3McNs4wcf3tIx8b5qoz09RvA\nPw/IbWcDwDsYMKnLeBowFpotn6cgsPrnots7qQ2tXDVPw3NZ8fEuSEDP0mLmh0sc\nZE4Q/dUZ2z8/MOiG5I+EVIw0ZNbPK0OQkmEJ3xksuaiTMvUN8CXr4bkWosm1C6dF\nH4bQNeDuXC1Hts2umXEjNBaiNcLlVIXBcYbllguZIIxcph0r/kKp9mEeH2bj5+dp\nV2c2PAhhgdPE67q/ebI+\n=VBKp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T18:26:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kubeflow/hub/commit/9c8ac43ed1596a713d2ea644acae44acb6029e53","node_id":"C_kwDOLEOEldoAKDljOGFjNDNlZDE1OTZhNzEzZDJlYTY0NGFjYWU0NGFjYjYwMjllNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kubeflow/hub/commit/509cfc7229ffee39cd1631329bdeb1e5760e710a","sha":"509cfc7229ffee39cd1631329bdeb1e5760e710a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/commits/509cfc7229ffee39cd1631329bdeb1e5760e710a"}],"sha":"9c8ac43ed1596a713d2ea644acae44acb6029e53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/commits/9c8ac43ed1596a713d2ea644acae44acb6029e53"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186957976?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DsThakurRawat","id":186957976,"login":"DsThakurRawat","node_id":"U_kgDOCyTAmA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DsThakurRawat","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/commits/509cfc7229ffee39cd1631329bdeb1e5760e710a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T17:54:09Z","email":"divyanshrawatofficial@gmail.com","name":"Divyansh Rawat"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T17:54:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(catalog): keep float precision in pagination cursors (#3213)\n\nA float sort value was written into the next-page token with 15\ndecimals, so any value needing more precision came back rounded and\nthe WHERE clause built from the cursor no longer matched the row the\ntoken pointed at. Ordering by a double custom property then repeated\nor skipped rows at page boundaries, and in descending order the token\nnever emptied.\n\nEncode the float with the shortest representation that parses back to\nthe same float64 instead.\n\nFixes #3212\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code\n\nSigned-off-by: Divyansh Rawat <divyanshrawatofficial@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"674a28dc1b6b89b7cf03a370dec266013cb3e9f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/git/trees/674a28dc1b6b89b7cf03a370dec266013cb3e9f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubeflow/hub/git/commits/509cfc7229ffee39cd1631329bdeb1e5760e710a","verification":{"payload":"tree 674a28dc1b6b89b7cf03a370dec266013cb3e9f0\nparent c083a4df8be89ff4fada179ae3d65316ca610e7b\nauthor Divyansh Rawat <divyanshrawatofficial@gmail.com> 1790099649 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790099649 +0000\n\nfix(catalog): keep float precision in pagination cursors (#3213)\n\nA float sort value was written into the next-page token with 15\ndecimals, so any value needing more precision came back rounded and\nthe WHERE clause built from the cursor no longer matched the row the\ntoken pointed at. Ordering by a double custom property then repeated\nor skipped rows at page boundaries, and in descending order the token\nnever emptied.\n\nEncode the float with the shortest representation that parses back to\nthe same float64 instead.\n\nFixes #3212\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code\n\nSigned-off-by: Divyansh Rawat <divyanshrawatofficial@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqssDBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL60QAAPvNcwcgqCTYE78n25LbMC1\nlAtGmAqhBBzG+deNsfBrnJGVEBx/i56PYRO3pmo5yAax+rYZNnXi/6UA28i2zkTN\n3pXh2iOk/TeU9DbtSLEHohuMajEjIR8QRF9Ts3P4TZ