cy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xIrusux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xIrusux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xIrusux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/xIrusux","id":42359615,"login":"xIrusux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMzU5NjE1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xIrusux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xIrusux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xIrusux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xIrusux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xIrusux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xIrusux","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/a6dfe603945d0ec442b7e0510e1a3c29ce1d659a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:45:20Z","email":"42359615+xIrusux@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Tine"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:45:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Element Tree] Restore nested node indentation (#4164)\n\n* [Element Tree] Restore nested node indentation\n\n#4056 turned the child list into a <ul> and reset its browser defaults with an inline\n`padding: 0`. Inline styles outrank the `.tree-node > .tree-list { padding-left }` rule that\nprovides the per-level indent, so every nested node rendered flush with the root.\n\nMove the ul reset into tree-list.styles so the indent rule in element-tree.styles applies again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Element Tree] Regression test for nested list indentation\n\nRenders the real tree with the authored CSS injected into jsdom and resolves padding-left the\nway a browser cascades it (inline wins, else the most specific matching rule). Fails on the\n#4056 inline `padding: 0` (every list 0px) and would fail again if the `.tree-node > .tree-list`\nindent rule were dropped. A root-level list outside any node stays at 0px.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"930aabdb9405dfe188064d35e12c49a94ddc24a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/trees/930aabdb9405dfe188064d35e12c49a94ddc24a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/commits/a6dfe603945d0ec442b7e0510e1a3c29ce1d659a","verification":{"payload":"tree 930aabdb9405dfe188064d35e12c49a94ddc24a0\nparent 8ee6a27da3f11b31a95f4940541f2a6720755270\nauthor Tine <42359615+xIrusux@users.noreply.github.com> 1791215120 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791215120 +0200\n\n[Element Tree] Restore nested node indentation (#4164)\n\n* [Element Tree] Restore nested node indentation\n\n#4056 turned the child list into a <ul> and reset its browser defaults with an inline\n`padding: 0`. Inline styles outrank the `.tree-node > .tree-list { padding-left }` rule that\nprovides the per-level indent, so every nested node rendered flush with the root.\n\nMove the ul reset into tree-list.styles so the indent rule in element-tree.styles applies again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Element Tree] Regression test for nested list indentation\n\nRenders the real tree with the authored CSS injected into jsdom and resolves padding-left the\nway a browser cascades it (inline wins, else the most specific matching rule). Fails on the\n#4056 inline `padding: 0` (every list 0px) and would fail again if the `.tree-node > .tree-list`\nindent rule were dropped. A root-level list outside any node stays at 0px.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.co