nts{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/1754617268061681259f9432f2941e73a50a5875","node_id":"C_kwDOLGAHt9oAKDE3NTQ2MTcyNjgwNjE2ODEyNTlmOTQzMmYyOTQxZTczYTUwYTU4NzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/07b02de6b065728a128704c9bea9eec68f03317b","sha":"07b02de6b065728a128704c9bea9eec68f03317b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/07b02de6b065728a128704c9bea9eec68f03317b"}],"sha":"1754617268061681259f9432f2941e73a50a5875","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/1754617268061681259f9432f2941e73a50a5875"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10495949?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sholzer","id":10495949,"login":"sholzer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDk1OTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sholzer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/07b02de6b065728a128704c9bea9eec68f03317b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:30:19Z","email":"sarah.holzer@pimcore.com","name":"Sarah Holzer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:30:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Main Navigation] Preview a group''s contents on hover (#4126)\n\n* [Main Navigation] Preview a group''s contents on hover (#2898)\n\nHovering a first-level main-nav group now opens it, so its entries can be\nscanned without a click. Levels below the root stay click-driven.\n\nThe open state (openKeys, the click handler and the hover preview) moves\ninto useNavOpenState; main-nav.tsx was already on the 300 line max-lines\ncap, so the hover code could not be added inline.\n\nDetails:\n- 120ms delay, so sweeping down the root column does not flash every group\n- mouse pointers only, leaving touch and pen on click\n- a re-hover of the open group keeps the deeper levels opened by click\n- hovering a root item without children closes the open panel\n- hover is ignored while a closed menu is still mounted for its fade-out,\n  which would otherwise rewrite openKeys from an invisible menu\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Main Navigation] Let a click win over the hover preview that preceded it\n\nA click is preceded by pointerenter, so clicking an already open root group\nwithin the 120ms preview delay closed it through the toggle and the pending\ntimer then reopened it. handleOpenState now cancels a pending preview first.\n\nReachable in normal use: openKeys survives closing the menu, so the group\nleft open is open again next time, and collapsing it means moving onto the\nrow and clicking it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: sholzer <10495949+sholzer@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf75daff60c2becd35c0a785816a2e0e8520e94d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/trees/cf75daff60c2becd35c0a785816a2e0e8520e94d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/commits/07b02de6b065728a128704c9bea9eec68f03317b","verification":{"payload":"tree cf75daff60c2becd35c0a785816a2e0e8520e94d\nparent 8f439ff272bc330554249f95a149b60c8b98ae34\nauthor Sarah Holzer <sarah.holzer@pimcore.com> 1790951419 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790951419 +0200\n\n[Main Navigation] Preview a group''s contents on hover (#4126)\n\n* [Main Navigation] Preview a group''s contents on hover (#2898)\n\nHovering a first-level main-nav group now opens it, so its entries can be\nscanned without a click. Levels below the root stay click-driven.\n\nThe open state (openKeys, the click handler and the hover preview) moves\ninto useNavOpenState; main-nav.tsx was already on the 300 line max-lines\ncap, so the hover code could not be added inline.\n\nDetails:\n- 120ms delay, so sweeping down the root column does not flash every group\n- mouse pointers only, leaving touch and pen on click\n- a re-hover of the open group keeps the deeper levels opened by click\n- hovering a root item without children closes the open panel\n- hover is ignored while a closed menu is still mounted for its fade-out,\n  which would otherwise rewrite openKeys from an invisible menu\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Main Navigation] Let a click win over the hover preview that preceded it\n\nA click is preceded by pointerenter, so clicking an already open root group\nwithin the 120ms preview delay closed it through the toggle and the pending\ntimer then reopened it. handleOpenState now cancels a pending preview first.\n\nReachable in normal use: openKeys survives closing the menu, so the group\nleft open is open again next time, and collapsing it means moving onto the\nrow and clicking it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: sholzer <10495949+sholzer@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv7/7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKYkQAKejNRJd8rRjfcws7b8ER4YA\nnkzlCPp7pJD6nGeg7Yd9xDwbp5Z255hxOIrZCGlDYFflrBkF7jCOKIgzoleOssXs\nj0asFQfTpCvujHiWGuyBhCDqPRHQsT3ku9pYXLWG1Tgb3uJRaefUHV2VSyyDltLR\n2QYvdwIbcZ2q4uB+Y8driMhzJqTS6r+um12xGjaEvynYnwLMN2ZLd2ETY3aUHgb8\nCXf03zmZ4YKVjVE5JogJ+jjfOy0z/EB+JdgpmOUYM5sUkiFDzKAjeqmfA3rQE3wy\n+AmnJdB9l8xLHYh0t8PaLFa2iq3l9gqAIBQbPsnbwODumgBBjpfgSOeJAcBeZ8az\nI1NlW3U/ndyz+iwMNHv592WJf54C4FfV/0AWoe+YQFfGxjupwVijxiry+pFcjUIp\nyGbNZAJu6tLT+bhRlIvP0JXjG0zIEdvBETOY3YKXn+bgguEEEMz3GdKVs/h3jST8\nK3onXnJGutlakYUw4qSiu6s3XWjuEmAj5z7s/q3XO2g2LiiInscaUGu/5GdooPhP\nTswWaqzdPg1MOIp3MR3L1p/AEe0W3rkW+gPcgzS22Q9ug6CFdUWR5Iq8yMLqlxaL\n98hpOS8XHIz26P2ZitMuy7BbBI7YFciGvKrj02DMCp0D8WRN9Ki0NdQ4hRQPq+S2\n4357UDxBgZyQCwzOeg0B\n=CLHq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T14:30:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","fo