}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/8f439ff272bc330554249f95a149b60c8b98ae34","node_id":"C_kwDOLGAHt9oAKDhmNDM5ZmYyNzJiYzMzMDU1NDI0OWY5NWExNDliNjBjOGI5OGFlMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/02fd618493ac26ac63259be3cc46666a8f9ec5a2","sha":"02fd618493ac26ac63259be3cc46666a8f9ec5a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/02fd618493ac26ac63259be3cc46666a8f9ec5a2"}],"sha":"8f439ff272bc330554249f95a149b60c8b98ae34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/8f439ff272bc330554249f95a149b60c8b98ae34"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138690998?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/idaiv","id":138690998,"login":"idaiv","node_id":"U_kgDOCERBtg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/02fd618493ac26ac63259be3cc46666a8f9ec5a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:53:26Z","email":"138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"idaiv"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:53:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Studio UI] Rewrite tree keyboard navigation with DOM-based traversal (#4048)\n\n* [Studio UI] Make tree nodes keyboard-reachable via roving tabindex\n\nTree nodes had tabIndex={-1}, making them unreachable via Tab key.\nApply roving tabindex: the selected node (or the first root node if\nnothing is selected) gets tabIndex={0}, all others stay at -1. Once\na node is focused, arrow keys already handle navigation.\n\nFixes WCAG 2.1 2.1.1 (Keyboard) — tree is now Tab-reachable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Rewrite tree keyboard navigation using DOM traversal\n\nReplace the broken nodeOrder()-based navigation with direct DOM\nquerySelectorAll traversal. The previous approach sorted internalKey\nstrings numerically which produced wrong ordering when parent keys\nwere prefixes of child keys.\n\nNew approach:\n- getAllTreeNodes() queries .tree-node__content-inner elements in the\n  actual DOM, guaranteeing correct visual order\n- Uses event.currentTarget instead of nodesRefs lookup, eliminating\n  stale ref mismatches\n- moveFocusToParent() walks up the DOM tree (.tree-node → .tree-list\n  → parent .tree-node) instead of comparing level numbers\n- Roving tabindex: selected or first node gets tabIndex=0\n- ArrowRight: expand if collapsed, move to first child if expanded\n- ArrowLeft: collapse if expanded, move to parent if collapsed\n- ArrowDown/Up: next/previous in visual order\n- Home/End: first/last visible node\n- aria-expanded on expandable nodes\n- focus-visible outline ring for keyboard users\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Reduce cognitive complexity in tree onKeyDown\n\nRefactor from chained if-statements to switch/case to reduce\ncognitive complexity flagged by SonarCloud.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Fix SonarCloud issues on tree keyboard navigation\n\n- Remove unused imports: KeyboardEvent, INodeRef\n- Move getVisibleNodes, moveFocus, moveFocusToParent to outer scope\n  (pure DOM functions, no component state dependency)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Tree keeps exactly one Tab stop; drop the status doc\n\n- The Tab stop moves to the tree container (useRovingTabStop): after nodes mount, unmount or change\n  selection, exactly one tree item has tabIndex 0 — the selected one while it is rendered, else the\n  first. The previous `isSelected || isFirstNode` read the node order from refs during render, before\n  the nodes had registered, so an unselected tree had no Tab stop until something re-rendered it.\n- Regression test with the real TreeNode (both root-display modes): one Tab stop in an unselected\n  tree, selecting another node moves it instead of adding one, and collapsing the selected node away\n  falls back to the first node.\n- docs/keyboard-accessibility-status.md removed: an internal status list, not documentation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e769ae575b5febf630a8968cdf5b9f1d2e90f59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/trees/9e769ae575b5febf630a8968cdf5b9f1d2e90f59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/commits/02fd618493ac26ac63259be3cc46666a8f9ec5a2","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e769ae575b5febf630a8968cdf5b9f1d2e90f59\nparent f427e73d54f25d9de445dde0634c87c44cd7234b\nauthor idaiv <138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com> 1790927606 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790927606 +0200\n\n[Studio UI] Rewrite tree keyboard navigation with DOM-based traversal (#4048)\n\n* [Studio UI] Make tree nodes keyboard-reachable via roving tabindex\n\nTree nodes had tabIndex={-1}, making them unreachable via Tab key.\nApply roving tabindex: the selected node (or the first root node if\nnothing is selected) gets tabIndex={0}, all others stay at -1. Once\na node is focused, arrow keys already handle navigation.\n\nFixes WCAG 2.1 2.1.1 (Keyboard) — tree is now Tab-reachable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Rewrite tree keyboard navigation using DOM traversal\n\nReplace the broken nodeOrder()-based navigation with direct DOM\nquerySelectorAll traversal. The previous approach sorted internalKey\nstrings numerically which produced wrong ordering when parent keys\nwere prefixes of child keys.\n\nNew approach:\n- getAllTreeNodes() queries .tree-node__content-inner elements in the\n  actual DOM, guaranteeing correct visual order\n- Uses event.currentTarget instead of nodesRefs lookup, eliminating\n  stale ref mismatches\n- moveFocusToParent() walks up the DOM tree (.tree-node → .tree-list\n  → parent .tree-node) instead of comparing level numbers\n- Roving tabindex: selected or first node gets tabIndex=0\n- ArrowRight: expand if collapsed, move to first child if expanded\n- ArrowLeft: collapse if expanded, move to parent if collapsed\n- ArrowDown/Up: next/previous in visual order\n- Home/End: first/last visible node\n- aria-expanded on expandable nodes\n- focus-visible outline ring for keyboard users\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Reduce cognitive complexity in tree onKeyDown\n\nRefactor from chained if-statements to switch/case to reduce\ncognitive complexity flagged by SonarCloud.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Fix SonarCloud issues on tree keyboard navigation\n\n- Remove unused imports: KeyboardEvent, INodeRef\n- Move getVisibleNodes, moveFocus, moveFocusToParent to outer scope\n  (pure DOM functions, no component state dependency)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Tree keeps exactly one Tab stop; drop the status doc\n\n- The Tab stop moves to the tree container (useRovingTabStop): after nodes mount, unmount or change\n  selection, exactly one tree item has tabIndex 0 — the selected one while it is rendered, else the\n  first. The previous `isSelected || isFirstNode` read the node order from refs during render, before\n  the nodes had registered, so an unselected tree had no Tab stop until something re-rendered it.\n- Regression test with the real TreeNode (both root-display modes): one Tab stop in an unselected\n  tree, selecting another node moves it instead of adding one, and collapsing the selected node away\n  falls back to the first node.\n- docs/keyboard-accessibility-status.md removed: an internal status list, not documentation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv2L2CRC1