/studio-ui-bundle/commit/f427e73d54f25d9de445dde0634c87c44cd7234b","sha":"f427e73d54f25d9de445dde0634c87c44cd7234b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/f427e73d54f25d9de445dde0634c87c44cd7234b"}],"sha":"02fd618493ac26ac63259be3cc46666a8f9ec5a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/02fd618493ac26ac63259be3cc46666a8f9ec5a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138690998?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/idaiv","id":138690998,"login":"idaiv","node_id":"U_kgDOCERBtg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/f427e73d54f25d9de445dde0634c87c44cd7234b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:53:06Z","email":"138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"idaiv"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:53:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Studio UI] Saved search grid UI improvements (#3836) (#4068)\n\n* [Studio UI] Add Header with saved search name to result widget (#3836)\n\nWhen a saved search is opened as a tab, the result widget now shows\na Header component with the saved search name as the title, following\nthe with-actions Header pattern. Uses position=\"top\" for the bottom\nborder separator.\n\nThe listing components (Asset/Object/Document) already provide:\n- Secondary toolbar with language switch (Object), refresh, pagination\n- TopBar with type select, class select, and search input\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Saved search grid UI improvements (#3836)\n\nHeader (TopBar):\n- When a saved search is opened as a tab, the TopBar now renders a\n  Header component (matching Redirects pattern) with the saved search\n  name as Title, type/class dropdowns alongside, and search input on\n  the right (width: 320px, matching SearchInput default)\n- Inside the search modal, the existing Toolbar layout is preserved\n\nToolbar (bottom):\n- Object listing: language switch on the LEFT, refresh + pagination\n  on the RIGHT when inside a saved search widget\n- Removed padding override — uses Toolbar''s default token.paddingXS\n- Inside the search modal, the original layout is preserved\n\nApplies to all three listing types (Asset, Document, Data Object).\n\nRelates to https://github.com/pimcore/product-management/issues/1448\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Address Copilot review: conditional padding + asset/document toolbars\n\n- Toolbar padding: conditionally apply padding={{ none }} only inside\n  the search modal, use default token.paddingXS in saved search widget\n- Asset and document toolbars: updated with same conditional padding\n  pattern and space-between layout (matching object toolbar)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Move saved-search top bar search sizing into shared styles file\n\nReplace the duplicated inline `style={ { width: 320, flexShrink: 0 } }`\nin the asset, document and data object saved-search top bars with a\nshared `searchContainer` class in\nmodal/tabs/shared/saved-search-top-bar.styles.ts, following the\nconvention of keeping component styles in dedicated createStyles files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a463386c4b935266b7267c713a5b4220de6b2ea5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/trees/a463386c4b935266b7267c713a5b4220de6b2ea5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/commits/f427e73d54f25d9de445dde0634c87c44cd7234b","verification":{"payload":"tree a463386c4b935266b7267c713a5b4220de6b2ea5\nparent 71d7466e4a05d1ee08738ee5c4cf0b9c66a75096\nauthor idaiv <138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com> 1790927586 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790927586 +0200\n\n[Studio UI] Saved search grid UI improvements (#3836) (#4068)\n\n* [Studio UI] Add Header with saved search name to result widget (#3836)\n\nWhen a saved search is opened as a tab, the result widget now shows\na Header component with the saved search name as the title, following\nthe with-actions Header pattern. Uses position=\"top\" for the bottom\nborder separator.\n\nThe listing components (Asset/Object/Document) already provide:\n- Secondary toolbar with language switch (Object), refresh, pagination\n- TopBar with type select, class select, and search input\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Saved search grid UI improvements (#3836)\n\nHeader (TopBar):\n- When a saved search is opened as a tab, the TopBar now renders a\n  Header component (matching Redirects pattern) with the saved search\n  name as Title, type/class dropdowns alongside, and search input on\n  the right (width: 320px, matching SearchInput default)\n- Inside the search modal, the existing Toolbar layout is preserved\n\nToolbar (bottom):\n- Object listing: language switch on the LEFT, refresh + pagination\n  on the RIGHT when inside a saved search widget\n- Removed padding override — uses Toolbar''s default token.paddingXS\n- Inside the search modal, the original layout is preserved\n\nApplies to all three listing types (Asset, Document, Data Object).\n\nRelates to https://github.com/pimcore/product-management/issues/1448\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Address Copilot review: conditional padding + asset/document toolbars\n\n- Toolbar padding: conditionally apply padding={{ none }} only inside\n  the search modal, use default token.paddingXS in saved search widget\n- Asset and document toolbars: updated with same conditional padding\n  pattern and space-between layout (matching object toolbar)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Move saved-search top bar search sizing into shared styles file\n\nReplace the duplicated inline `style={ { width: 320, flexShrink: 0 } }`\nin the asset, document and data object saved-search top bars with a\nshared `searchContainer` class in\nmodal/tabs/shared/saved-search-top-bar.styles.ts, following the\nconvention of keeping component styles in dedicated createStyles files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv2LiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgXkQAAq+mBS79DW/bfZxhqCSNp/e\njVJKKTK0q0OxcBkpp7Fp1jhQaYJnnodzRkykIB6Zo/IVZAh5nUCTcHTcueB70sd1\nDdgcu6X8tae1zhAlg9Wdp1Ft8yujcdJnIVNLB8ecG36sObFuYQNfLwKrfgNHkZbZ\nFjuOGA57mFXNi8EI3KGyHKZOqFivTkYKQITzxt1PpDC58CVaqIHt0WCSffEf98rA\nX4SDG6LL7kNGbuSlrW+Qn2wZjy/ism19lAEdSdZ60qXD4yQD84upqCF7hxiA7ZrL\nDjEpnFc/mVuUufUgbzNWutxaeG1L5JMk8lpGQrS0m3Nf1kIHMlVw32zHA7Z3cJr/\nWBkt