"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/5e23ce44598d55fb1c41b617740686f3db5dfc1d","node_id":"C_kwDOLGAHt9oAKDVlMjNjZTQ0NTk4ZDU1ZmIxYzQxYjYxNzc0MDY4NmYzZGI1ZGZjMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/49f5a9b0aa0b118fbe5992ea759d2c1b9b32a01d","sha":"49f5a9b0aa0b118fbe5992ea759d2c1b9b32a01d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/49f5a9b0aa0b118fbe5992ea759d2c1b9b32a01d"}],"sha":"5e23ce44598d55fb1c41b617740686f3db5dfc1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/5e23ce44598d55fb1c41b617740686f3db5dfc1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138690998?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/idaiv","id":138690998,"login":"idaiv","node_id":"U_kgDOCERBtg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/49f5a9b0aa0b118fbe5992ea759d2c1b9b32a01d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:35:04Z","email":"138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"idaiv"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:35:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Studio UI] Keep Tab navigation within grid bounds (#4060)\n\n* [Studio UI] Keep Tab navigation within grid bounds\n\nTab/Shift+Tab now move between cells within the grid: Tab moves to\nthe next cell (wrapping to the first cell of the next row), Shift+Tab\nto the previous. Tab only exits the grid at the very first or last\ncell, matching the WAI-ARIA grid pattern.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Reduce cognitive complexity in grid keyboard navigation\n\nExtract resolveTarget and resolveTabTarget from handleArrowNavigation\nto bring cognitive complexity from 16 to within the allowed 15.\nUses switch/case for cleaner key dispatch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Only intercept Tab when target grid cell is focusable\n\nCustom cells such as the selection checkbox do not render the\ndata-grid-* navigation attributes, so Tab/Shift+Tab towards them called\npreventDefault() and then failed to find a target, trapping focus.\nNow the target element is resolved first and Tab falls back to native\nbrowser behavior when no navigable cell exists.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d3bfe113a28ad0101ce56fd0bff2b69f6dc4924","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/trees/1d3bfe113a28ad0101ce56fd0bff2b69f6dc4924"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/commits/49f5a9b0aa0b118fbe5992ea759d2c1b9b32a01d","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d3bfe113a28ad0101ce56fd0bff2b69f6dc4924\nparent 5365dbc33b155127454d5fa873cb2331444da81c\nauthor idaiv <138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com> 1790861704 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790861704 +0200\n\n[Studio UI] Keep Tab navigation within grid bounds (#4060)\n\n* [Studio UI] Keep Tab navigation within grid bounds\n\nTab/Shift+Tab now move between cells within the grid: Tab moves to\nthe next cell (wrapping to the first cell of the next row), Shift+Tab\nto the previous. Tab only exits the grid at the very first or last\ncell, matching the WAI-ARIA grid pattern.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Reduce cognitive complexity in grid keyboard navigation\n\nExtract resolveTarget and resolveTabTarget from handleArrowNavigation\nto bring cognitive complexity from 16 to within the allowed 15.\nUses switch/case for cleaner key dispatch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Only intercept Tab when target grid cell is focusable\n\nCustom cells such as the selection checkbox do not render the\ndata-grid-* navigation attributes, so Tab/Shift+Tab towards them called\npreventDefault() and then failed to find a target, trapping focus.\nNow the target element is resolved first and Tab falls back to native\nbrowser behavior when no navigable cell exists.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvmGICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPJIQAK0xgb694PZLLL3pBsWrDlwd\npxj6SjOA/SK+izaZ771CR5wHgmhzo/h2dbCcAVLtH74GUJzJXEghsFv6k+b9A99c\n2EeoR61uUAIS6HD7xnzZAOvX5W9PpxsvSyHaRFupNtOvg3rGWXTORubHwTO0XHea\n3b6QTrBo+2IJoPL8LHpbItu8epN3a2u/N2ODbHVDkWZhsM5t+0h/gmH2Jp7XXlNC\nLJxrOwwAY9RNYPdnt9NqOVdCOZImjdHUA497uCoDc73eLgjKKpEkhRFf4sZ99mRx\neiHqLFctCk59GtHDbjtm2AOfi6SLVLROmg2OR7RlShu8bybH3sMiSbiHaKGhIsws\nqBozyEbYUCrmsNoMN20Er9ZPaqDMSo9YUavm4FMixuUYiC3t0J8lYEODOd9gdYpk\nnRjkVMLH65F3uvek8X/FSHcpmp6033TF0XesmxrDeJ+qhWsn5HlU9hwP9wgI9sdA\nJ2OwbuBoN92P9p8WujZ/2NMML4fxdURkrP2LNZiMVqgSHPhcUm/AHOHWovqVnLnn\nfk0Sgj3LMnFdTdyoAl43pPkXJGJWR/IzSjdpmPjp3sJoWxzim4RSt2AmqwWGg6I7\nzcg6Q42MOLzWJUxft7Ch6bHfFwFX2aSgQzwdXMj13Zmwwd3qBapNTQVY20rldsDb\nVV5YAiO2PLwviGWAHHwT\n=7yqE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T13:35:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/49f5a9b0aa0b118fbe5992ea759d2c1b9b32a01d","node_id":"C_kwDOLGAHt9oAKDQ5ZjVhOWIwYWEwYjExOGZiZTU5OTJlYTc1OWQyYzFiOWIzMmEwMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/5365dbc33b155127454d5fa873cb2331444da81c","sha":"5365dbc33b155127454d5fa873cb2331444da81c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/5365dbc33b155127454d5fa873cb2331444da81c"}],"sha":"49f5a9b0aa0b118fbe5992ea759d2c1b9b32a01d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/49f5a9b0aa0b118fbe5992ea759d2c1b9b32a01d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138690998?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/idaiv","id":138690998,"login":"idaiv","node_id":"U_kgDOCERBtg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/5365dbc33b155127454d5fa873cb2331444da81c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:34:34Z","email":"138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"idaiv"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:34:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Studio UI] Align action labels with the add/new and delete/remove rules (#4043)\n\n* [Studio UI] Align action labels with the add/new and delete/remove rules\n\nApplies the labelling rules from #645 to wording that still contradicted them,\nwithout touching casing — #4031 already settled that, and its Title Case for\ncontext menus is preserved.\n\nAdd vs New. Eleven creation dialogs were labelled \"Add new ...\" or\n\"Create new ...\", using both verbs at once or one the ruleset does not define.\nThe ruleset gives \"New\" for creating from scratch, in a modal included, so they\nnow read \"New object of type X\", \"New user\", \"New class definition\" and so on.\nThe icons already agreed with this — folder-plus, shield-plus and an add-user\nglyph that is a person with a plus — so the words were the only mismatch.\n\nDelete vs Remove. Five actions rendered a trash icon, called a delete endpoint\nand warned that the action cannot be undone, while their label said Remove:\nthe site tree action, the folder tree action, both thumbnail transformation\nlists and the notification toolbar. Their tree-action siblings already read\n\"Delete user\" and \"Delete role\", so \"Delete\" is what matches both the icon and\nthe neighbouring wording. The site dialog''s confirmation text and confirm\nbutton, and the folder and user success messages, are aligned with it.\n\nUntouched: tags, crop and bulk-import removals, which genuinely leave the thing\nin the system, and \"Create\" on modal confirm buttons, which the ruleset does not\ncover and the codebase applies consistently.\n\nAlso adds roles.remove-folder, user-management.remove-folder and their .text\ncounterparts. Both folder-delete modals reference them, but they were missing\nfrom all seven locale files, so the dialog rendered the raw keys as its title\nand body.\n\nRefs #645\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Sync translations with studio.en.yaml [automated]\n\n* Review fixes: keep context-menu Title Case and Swedish site terminology\n\ntree.actions.remove-folder is a tree context-menu item, so it keeps Title Case\nper #4031 — the verb change should not have altered casing, which the PR\ndescription itself said it would not.\n\nThe Swedish site strings use \"sajt\", as its siblings use-as-site and edit-site\nalready do; \"webbplats\" introduced a second term for the same noun. Swedish is\nthe only locale where this drifted — every other one already matched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Sync translations with studio.en.yaml [automated]\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: pimcore-deployments <71881008+pimcore-deployments@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b5e56d8fa81a34a541a51d9b7aecc021abfb7f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/trees/2b5e56d8fa81a34a541a51d9b7aecc021abfb7f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/commits/5365dbc33b155127454d5fa873cb2331444da81c","verification":{"payload":"tree 2b5e56d8fa81a34a541a51d9b7aecc021abfb7f2\nparent 7b1820abf39034bfdb081525c3988370b1e14e18\nauthor idaiv <138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com> 1790861674 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790861674 +0200\n\n[Studio UI] Align action labels with the add/new and delete/remove rules (#4043)\n\n* [Studio UI] Align action labels with the add/new and delete/remove rules\n\nApplies the labelling rules from #645 to wording that still contradicted them,\nwithout touching casing — #4031 already settled that, and its Title Case for\ncontext menus is preserved.\n\nAdd vs New. Eleven creation dialogs were labelled \"Add new ...\" or\n\"Create new ...\", using both verbs at once or one the ruleset does not define.\nThe ruleset gives \"New\" for creating from scratch, in a modal included, so they\nnow read \"New object of type X\", \"New user\", \"New class definition\" and so on.\nThe icons already agreed with this — folder-plus, shield-plus and an add-user\nglyph that is a person with a plus — so the words were the only mismatch.\n\nDelete vs Remove. Five actions rendered a trash icon, called a delete endpoint\nand warned that the action cannot be undone, while their label said Remove:\nthe site tree action, the folder tree action, both thumbnail transformation\nlists and the notification toolbar. Their tree-action siblings already read\n\"Delete user\" and \"Delete role\", so \"Delete\" is what matches both the icon and\nthe neighbouring wording. The site dialog''s confirmation text and confirm\nbutton, and the folder and user success messages, are aligned with it.\n\nUntouched: tags, crop and bulk-import removals, which genuinely leave the thing\nin the system, and \"Create\" on modal confirm buttons, which the ruleset does not\ncover and the codebase applies consistently.\n\nAlso adds roles.remove-folder, user-management.remove-folder and their .text\ncounterparts. Both folder-delete modals reference them, but they were missing\nfrom all seven locale files, so the dialog rendered the raw keys as its title\nand body.\n\nRefs #645\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Sync translations with studio.en.yaml [automated]\n\n* Review fixes: keep context-menu Title Case and Swedish site terminology\n\ntree.actions.remove-folder is a tree context-menu item, so it keeps Title Case\nper #4031 — the verb change should not have altered casing, which the PR\ndescription itself said it would not.\n\nThe Swedish site strings use \"sajt\", as its siblings use-as-site and edit-site\nalready do; \"webbplats\" introduced a second term for the same noun. Swedish is\nthe only locale where this drifted — every other one already matched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Sync translations with studio.en.yaml [automated]\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: pimcore-deployments <71881008+pimcore-deployments@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvmFqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8GsQAIQqDIt/56YAnmp1gKx658r+\nxby+jFQTVKPk8B78jHbqj1SBnRasZ3xkE9jBvovwmKOmG9k6cy0myoS8TvZOJrec\nzv3KAnFiF/Co9wMdMmPTWkjVUN5IdOUv/vief+90eKA3NMc0+1iXUBRU+yDyIimD\nTzszWg4xzImDvzHd3qq7p2iJgwgO0VaS61aiNd2l8fldQpxDlsXYcWkL9IqyNzY6\nDgNIa0iUrIs9ou575wvqUBSExoBTf+wbWKzcGeo8zcDVtRoex3Mma8zTPIJEm8On\nGJnUhuq0XFkSE2eReVYo5CApDhjAK5qDKwOcKR/BhEUwpB/S86FPhiir7CL8IFM3\nbpHEnpQwFg2eKMJ2DhblbvU4cqP62zD+wuCeuDdW/ogEatCCloPHaxnFV0wn6nT0\n7nG1y+2OBx3yIX0UW4Tb6hUU66zT1fw/oBJJxrIkR7d+D8ZCMJS2/yPoWYpgv1Qt\n/pU79V1L7TGYgcKvE+AvKUQGkSrI8rOiX69KBCouTRzr+kBJedSIu7CT77ALA64Y\nf5bceN5CXcV/T8N96WKdEbJXm6+Je9PIxxLFe2NLrgjk7NDv6/HpjKB67jVheNtu\n6ft3RFfa/sQMutlUUdEQLHpdXP5NZVZ8vd9YO8Aa1hW2wyvwo5iHmAIXB8IsJ3KD\nCtoEtNJjhcGAvG0JFwm4\n=I/Hm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T13:34:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false