"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/0672b2c2cbd7b3e0467f45b67ae104f42fa96cca","sha":"0672b2c2cbd7b3e0467f45b67ae104f42fa96cca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/0672b2c2cbd7b3e0467f45b67ae104f42fa96cca"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/eba281856bc3e8729b69ba6d8e8e83807fa66b7e","sha":"eba281856bc3e8729b69ba6d8e8e83807fa66b7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/eba281856bc3e8729b69ba6d8e8e83807fa66b7e"}],"sha":"e31fd7f20da646793e7c09b716854cdeaa3b0672","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/e31fd7f20da646793e7c09b716854cdeaa3b0672"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138690998?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/idaiv","id":138690998,"login":"idaiv","node_id":"U_kgDOCERBtg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/idaiv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/0672b2c2cbd7b3e0467f45b67ae104f42fa96cca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T07:30:55Z","email":"138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com","name":"idaiv"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T07:30:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Studio UI] Add WAI-ARIA tree roles to element tree (#4056)\n\n* [Studio UI] Add WAI-ARIA tree roles to element tree\n\n- Container: role=\"tree\"\n- Nodes: role=\"treeitem\" (replaces role=\"button\")\n- Child lists: role=\"group\"\n- aria-expanded on expandable nodes\n- aria-selected on all nodes\n- aria-level reflecting nesting depth\n\nScreen readers can now identify the tree structure, announce folder\nstate, selection, and depth. Completes WCAG 2.1 4.1.2 (Name, Role,\nValue) for tree components.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Fix aria-level minimum value for root node\n\nRoot node has level={-1}, producing aria-level={0} which is invalid\n(WAI-ARIA minimum is 1). Clamp to Math.max(1, level + 1).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Add aria-label to tree containers\n\nEach tree instance (Asset, Document, Data Object) now passes a\ntranslated aria-label to the role=\"tree\" container so screen readers\ncan distinguish between multiple trees on screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Use ul element for tree group to satisfy SonarCloud S6819\n\nSonarCloud flags role=\"group\" on a div. Use a ul element instead\nwhich is semantically appropriate for a list of tree items and\nsatisfies the rule while maintaining the WAI-ARIA tree pattern.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Remove explicit role=group to fix SonarCloud S6819\n\nSonarCloud S6819 only accepts <details>, <fieldset>, <optgroup>, or\n<address> for the group role — none appropriate for a tree. The\nsemantic <ul> element inside a role=\"tree\" container is already\nunderstood by assistive technology as a grouping, so the explicit\nrole attribute is unnecessary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Derive tree aria-level from root visibility\n\nWhen the root node is shown it is rendered with level -1 and its children\nwith level 0, so clamping aria-level to 1 gave the root and its children\nthe same level. Expose hasRootNode via TreeContext and offset aria-level\naccordingly so levels start at 1 and increment with depth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ad83d9466e03e8fd343d1fc8dd840fe02c78da4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/trees/ad83d9466e03e8fd343d1fc8dd840fe02c78da4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/commits/0672b2c2cbd7b3e0467f45b67ae104f42fa96cca","verification":{"payload":"tree ad83d9466e03e8fd343d1fc8dd840fe02c78da4e\nparent e4c81a0d13d1840c98b852a032d964e83a818b96\nauthor idaiv <138690998+idaiv@users.noreply.github.com> 1790839855 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790839855 +0200\n\n[Studio UI] Add WAI-ARIA tree roles to element tree (#4056)\n\n* [Studio UI] Add WAI-ARIA tree roles to element tree\n\n- Container: role=\"tree\"\n- Nodes: role=\"treeitem\" (replaces role=\"button\")\n- Child lists: role=\"group\"\n- aria-expanded on expandable nodes\n- aria-selected on all nodes\n- aria-level reflecting nesting depth\n\nScreen readers can now identify the tree structure, announce folder\nstate, selection, and depth. Completes WCAG 2.1 4.1.2 (Name, Role,\nValue) for tree components.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Fix aria-level minimum value for root node\n\nRoot node has level={-1}, producing aria-level={0} which is invalid\n(WAI-ARIA minimum is 1). Clamp to Math.max(1, level + 1).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Add aria-label to tree containers\n\nEach tree instance (Asset, Document, Data Object) now passes a\ntranslated aria-label to the role=\"tree\" container so screen readers\ncan distinguish between multiple trees on screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Use ul element for tree group to satisfy SonarCloud S6819\n\nSonarCloud flags role=\"group\" on a div. Use a ul element instead\nwhich is semantically appropriate for a list of tree items and\nsatisfies the rule while maintaining the WAI-ARIA tree pattern.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Remove explicit role=group to fix SonarCloud S6819\n\nSonarCloud S6819 only accepts <details>, <fieldset>, <optgroup>, or\n<address> for the group role — none appropriate for a tree. The\nsemantic <ul> element inside a role=\"tree\" container is already\nunderstood by assistive technology as a grouping, so the explicit\nrole attribute is unnecessary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Studio UI] Derive tree aria-level from root visibility\n\nWhen the root node is shown it is rendered with level -1 and its children\nwith level 0, so clamping aria-level to 1 gave the root and its children\nthe same level. Expose hasRootNode via TreeContext and offset aria-level\naccordingly so levels start at 1 and increment with depth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvgwvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAabAQAD/4/tDzutWhbaePfuilpUZQ\nC55V/aA/b0KmbTx0VubJcEn/XgURUVpV/fcwjGM8jkmjFGbE65atxWQn7sugXUkM\n4hrUjq9qLfKyTOAujALHe824uM5iYTZgF+oGDw1RDAXEDXs7z7SLKjIsDz2kVnLd