tps://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/20ab703a2b4e6d48aaf1ed46a6f02dc486229278","node_id":"C_kwDOLGAHt9oAKDIwYWI3MDNhMmI0ZTZkNDhhYWYxZWQ0NmE2ZjAyZGM0ODYyMjkyNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commit/9830bc3b0b79bce53b2d21bb1b21cbd20890ad6d","sha":"9830bc3b0b79bce53b2d21bb1b21cbd20890ad6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/9830bc3b0b79bce53b2d21bb1b21cbd20890ad6d"}],"sha":"20ab703a2b4e6d48aaf1ed46a6f02dc486229278","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/20ab703a2b4e6d48aaf1ed46a6f02dc486229278"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4639428?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus-moser/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus-moser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus-moser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus-moser/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/markus-moser","id":4639428,"login":"markus-moser","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2Mzk0Mjg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus-moser/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus-moser/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus-moser/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus-moser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus-moser/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markus-moser","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/commits/9830bc3b0b79bce53b2d21bb1b21cbd20890ad6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:23:52Z","email":"markus.moser@pimcore.com","name":"markus-moser"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:23:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Search] Host a search listing outside the modal, and keep a restored search''s columns (#4095)\n\n* [Listing] A search listing can be hosted, not only opened from the search modal\n\nA host outside the modal needs to say which sidebar entry opens, add its\nown entries, show the saved-search panel without its write actions, and\nmount a logic-only companion inside the listing''s provider tree. The\npanel''s live form values reach the provider, so a host can read the draft\nit is editing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Saved Search] Restoring a search keeps the columns it saved\n\nThree ways the saved layout was lost. Both column loaders re-applied the\nclass defaults on every refetch and on StrictMode''s second pass, which\noverwrote a restored layout after it landed; the quick-search loader also\nhas to defer to a loaded search that owns its class''s columns. The restore\nconsumed itself against the classless column set — a class loads its own\ncolumns only after the class selection and the type select that the\nrestore itself applies — so class data columns mapped away. And a column\nsaved without a locale carried undefined where grid data carries null, so\nthe column mappers matched no value and its cells rendered empty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Saved Search] The panel publishes the users and roles a search is shared with\n\nThey are picked in a dropdown rather than in the form, so a host mirroring\nthe panel saw every sharing change except that one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Saved Search] A search that names no columns still gets applied\n\nThe restore treats \"the grid carries the saved columns\" as proof it has\nrun, so a search with no column list satisfied that on the first tick and\nwas consumed having applied nothing — its filter, type select and page\nsize never reached the grid, which then showed everything. It now applies\nonce per pending search before the column match can stand in for it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Drop the local build lock file that was committed by accident\n\npublic/.studio-build-extract.lock is a build artefact: untracked on 2026.x and\nin no .gitignore, so `git add -A` picks it up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] The column loaders apply each response once, not each configuration once\n\nKeying the guard on class and configuration skipped a refetch that brought new\ndata (the favourite after a delete) and, on a class switch, recorded a pair of\ntwo classes'' answers and then skipped the right one. The guard now remembers the\nresponse objects and reads currentData, which is empty while the arguments move.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A saved search is restored once its whole layout holds, on its class''s columns\n\nThe convergence check compared keys only, so a late write that reset a column''s\nlocale or width passed as restored. Class readiness was inferred from a non-system\ncolumn being available, which never happens for a class without data fields; the\nrestore now waits until the listing carries exactly the class''s column set.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] Inline sidebar entries no longer remount a hosted search listing\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] The saved-search panel draft has a type of its own\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Sidebar] A default tab can be collapsed like any other\n\nWithout a provider the default was already open on the first pass, so it was never\nmarked handled and collapsing it opened it again. Tests and a story for the prop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nThe previous archive packaged a development build''s leftovers and source maps.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A saved search holds a class''s columns only while it is being restored\n\nKeyed on the loaded search, the hold lasted for the life of the tab: switching\nclass and back kept the other class''s columns in the grid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] Class defaults stand in when none of a saved search''s columns exist\n\nA search whose columns all left the class still held the selection, and the\nrestore could install nothing, so the classless columns stayed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] SearchProvider memoizes its value, not the element it renders\n\nA host that swapped the hosted listing while the search state held kept\nrendering the old one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A class changed mid-restore is set back to the saved one\n\nThe class effect never ran again, so the restore waited at its class gate and\nstayed pending.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A restore whose layout already holds is consumed after its first apply\n\nThe first pass applied the search and returned; when nothing it changed was a\ndependency of the effect, the effect never ran again and the restore stayed\npending — a search naming no columns among them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A restore applies once per configuration, and again when handed back\n\nThe asset and document restore re-applied the whole search when its own column\nupdate landed, reloading twice. Both restores now remember what they applied\nand forget it once nothing is pending, so a host passing the same object back\ngets it applied again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A Save panel takes its draft back when it unmounts\n\nThe draft outlived the panel that published it, so a host that swapped the\nlisting kept reading values from a form that no longer existed. It is cleared\nonly while it is still that panel''s, so a sibling panel''s draft survives.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Search] The panel draft is the shown panel''s\n\nThe search modal keeps visited tabs mounted, so the draft belonged to whichever\npanel wrote last, and an unselected tab could overwrite the selected one''s. In\nthe open modal only the selected tab''s panel publishes, and it republishes when\nits tab is selected again; outside the modal the panel is the only one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] Empty and undefined checks use lodash\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A saved search whose class was deleted restores classless\n\nIts class can never be selected, so the restore waited at the class gate for\ngood. Once the class catalog has loaded without the class, the search restores\nagainst the classless columns, as it did before the restore waited for its class.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A deleted-class search drops a stale class before restoring classless\n\nThe restore stopped waiting for the missing class but still applied against\nwhatever class was selected. It now clears that selection first and applies once\nthe listing is classless; a listing offering a single class has no classless\nstate and restores against that one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] The Save form checks for an undefined value with lodash\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] Drop the imports left behind when the layout helpers moved out\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] Test the saved-search restore against every order its inputs can arrive in\n\nThe object restore is played against the real column loaders for every order of\nthe search being handed in, the class catalog, the classless configuration, the\nclass''s columns and configuration, and the consumption hold; the asset and\ndocument restore against the real static configuration it is mounted under. Each\nrun must be consumed only once the grid carries the saved layout on its final\ncolumn set, with nothing but the restore replacing the columns meanwhile.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: markus-moser <4639428+markus-moser@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd9fe7a8cf89b0fac43df55d754ba03844881efc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/trees/cd9fe7a8cf89b0fac43df55d754ba03844881efc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-ui-bundle/git/commits/9830bc3b0b79bce53b2d21bb1b21cbd20890ad6d","verification":{"payload":"tree cd9fe7a8cf89b0fac43df55d754ba03844881efc\nparent 3f4158a27e530893aa4dbd1c3d4171c861d2f08a\nauthor markus-moser <markus.moser@pimcore.com> 1790756632 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790756632 +0200\n\n[Search] Host a search listing outside the modal, and keep a restored search''s columns (#4095)\n\n* [Listing] A search listing can be hosted, not only opened from the search modal\n\nA host outside the modal needs to say which sidebar entry opens, add its\nown entries, show the saved-search panel without its write actions, and\nmount a logic-only companion inside the listing''s provider tree. The\npanel''s live form values reach the provider, so a host can read the draft\nit is editing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Saved Search] Restoring a search keeps the columns it saved\n\nThree ways the saved layout was lost. Both column loaders re-applied the\nclass defaults on every refetch and on StrictMode''s second pass, which\noverwrote a restored layout after it landed; the quick-search loader also\nhas to defer to a loaded search that owns its class''s columns. The restore\nconsumed itself against the classless column set — a class loads its own\ncolumns only after the class selection and the type select that the\nrestore itself applies — so class data columns mapped away. And a column\nsaved without a locale carried undefined where grid data carries null, so\nthe column mappers matched no value and its cells rendered empty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Saved Search] The panel publishes the users and roles a search is shared with\n\nThey are picked in a dropdown rather than in the form, so a host mirroring\nthe panel saw every sharing change except that one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Saved Search] A search that names no columns still gets applied\n\nThe restore treats \"the grid carries the saved columns\" as proof it has\nrun, so a search with no column list satisfied that on the first tick and\nwas consumed having applied nothing — its filter, type select and page\nsize never reached the grid, which then showed everything. It now applies\nonce per pending search before the column match can stand in for it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* Drop the local build lock file that was committed by accident\n\npublic/.studio-build-extract.lock is a build artefact: untracked on 2026.x and\nin no .gitignore, so `git add -A` picks it up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] The column loaders apply each response once, not each configuration once\n\nKeying the guard on class and configuration skipped a refetch that brought new\ndata (the favourite after a delete) and, on a class switch, recorded a pair of\ntwo classes'' answers and then skipped the right one. The guard now remembers the\nresponse objects and reads currentData, which is empty while the arguments move.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A saved search is restored once its whole layout holds, on its class''s columns\n\nThe convergence check compared keys only, so a late write that reset a column''s\nlocale or width passed as restored. Class readiness was inferred from a non-system\ncolumn being available, which never happens for a class without data fields; the\nrestore now waits until the listing carries exactly the class''s column set.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] Inline sidebar entries no longer remount a hosted search listing\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] The saved-search panel draft has a type of its own\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Sidebar] A default tab can be collapsed like any other\n\nWithout a provider the default was already open on the first pass, so it was never\nmarked handled and collapsing it opened it again. Tests and a story for the prop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nThe previous archive packaged a development build''s leftovers and source maps.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A saved search holds a class''s columns only while it is being restored\n\nKeyed on the loaded search, the hold lasted for the life of the tab: switching\nclass and back kept the other class''s columns in the grid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] Class defaults stand in when none of a saved search''s columns exist\n\nA search whose columns all left the class still held the selection, and the\nrestore could install nothing, so the classless columns stayed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] SearchProvider memoizes its value, not the element it renders\n\nA host that swapped the hosted listing while the search state held kept\nrendering the old one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A class changed mid-restore is set back to the saved one\n\nThe class effect never ran again, so the restore waited at its class gate and\nstayed pending.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A restore whose layout already holds is consumed after its first apply\n\nThe first pass applied the search and returned; when nothing it changed was a\ndependency of the effect, the effect never ran again and the restore stayed\npending — a search naming no columns among them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A restore applies once per configuration, and again when handed back\n\nThe asset and document restore re-applied the whole search when its own column\nupdate landed, reloading twice. Both restores now remember what they applied\nand forget it once nothing is pending, so a host passing the same object back\ngets it applied again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A Save panel takes its draft back when it unmounts\n\nThe draft outlived the panel that published it, so a host that swapped the\nlisting kept reading values from a form that no longer existed. It is cleared\nonly while it is still that panel''s, so a sibling panel''s draft survives.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Automatic frontend build\n\n* [Search] The panel draft is the shown panel''s\n\nThe search modal keeps visited tabs mounted, so the draft belonged to whichever\npanel wrote last, and an unselected tab could overwrite the selected one''s. In\nthe open modal only the selected tab''s panel publishes, and it republishes when\nits tab is selected again; outside the modal the panel is the only one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] Empty and undefined checks use lodash\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A saved search whose class was deleted restores classless\n\nIts class can never be selected, so the restore waited at the class gate for\ngood. Once the class catalog has loaded without the class, the search restores\nagainst the classless columns, as it did before the restore waited for its class.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] A deleted-class search drops a stale class before restoring classless\n\nThe restore stopped waiting for the missing class but still applied against\nwhatever class was selected. It now clears that selection first and applies once\nthe listing is classless; a listing offering a single class has no classless\nstate and restores against that one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] The Save form checks for an undefined value with lodash\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] Drop the imports left behind when the layout helpers moved out\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [Search] Test the saved-search restore against every order its inputs can arrive in\n\nThe object restore is played against the real column loaders for every order of\nthe search being handed in, the class catalog, the classless configuration, the\nclass''s columns and configuration, and the consumption hold; the asset and\ndocument restore against the real static configuration it is mounted under. Each\nrun must be consumed only once the grid carries the saved layout on its final\ncolumn set, with nothing but the restore replacing the columns meanwhile.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Frontend build\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: markus-moser <4639428+markus-moser@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvMcYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu+EQALHZ9ywz7BPFquj0Vkg1glDu\n1FEH+edrL7tnrFZiy6IriXlSbaGAz49KP8R1jlL9JGWSEucjR77aI+q2NDblayAk\nngL4K75Mc6edSgpeygEJ2SY+NXtrnQRaoAa4hlIqPcjNISHNKPrw0qQYTl72NUZ1\nFMMZXXCfSyF2nxVACQ5PIb1GgLwpT3pXQqlFT+v/S7VJA4U/r5z6+yoSPiictmtu\nTfqp37jTGEj9BvOY2PAinnS2l/ZPXokm4GAj0Wm2WMVpGSkf61KSGs14+fmBJeae\nlipzrdJ1jZJofuf7J5H4SkryJkZb1NVBIz6PqoMMsNWRG4kYkhF0ZefpdsqW56Kw\n7LPUf9FVPRCIzGmfLv1jGJcB3Z+GBzb0/D8q84e1cXz9w4Ux5gW07wkYkxkIVKVR\nk3krC0FltWJcEFWdtWwieCt+7mIHJ7u7MJwzDl6GA1e6MPhr1FNIcJ1OOLMRojEc\nIKebsdbzeoazp0dBI4tgrVXM0qKHVuRFsTn7F+Ck3qbrz3kZHJrT+S+xvl7+oj7K\nlWqg9MZp5Xk+7O6gR1toFw8PPf/pI6sX5Ic+Hk2y9iwQAzewC0OpdFPfE59zcqSQ\n3po+3w5JQ8zbNbRINE0u/J/2FbtuagjrxFcbYxU0iAonKPnwoI6KjYJwnD8UKyk7\nRGzt2UhKxmAxfSYuo42c\n=MW46\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T08:23:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.co