e,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/commits/d47d5b42a97d32af097d9cff0b1a73231e0ef0a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T10:44:00Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T10:44:00Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v3.2.0\n\n- (@GermanBluefox) The live widget for `ioBroker.devices` still tried the stream relative to admin (port 8081) when the adapter did not report the address of the web instance in time. Without an address the widget now takes single pictures over the socket and tells the reason in the browser console; an address that arrives late still switches to the stream\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added the names Frigate recognizes (face recognition, known license plates): `<zone>.sub_labels` lists the names in a zone right now, and `sub_labels.<name>` is `true` as long as a running event carries that name. With face recognition enabled, the names of the face library are created on start, so automations can be set up before somebody is recognized for the first time (#277)\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed repochecker warnings: literal placeholders of the settings dialog are in the translation files, and dependabot also watches `src-devices`","tree":{"sha":"e9ca6e4003b36f9c7a97c40ad1efa1cf98e4f800","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/git/trees/e9ca6e4003b36f9c7a97c40ad1efa1cf98e4f800"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/git/commits/d47d5b42a97d32af097d9cff0b1a73231e0ef0a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verifie