s/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/commits/a571109d94e05e00605d7ede3d00a176d02a0347/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:53:35Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:53:35Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v3.1.2\n\n- (@GermanBluefox) The Frigate directory can no longer be left empty by accident: the validator complained but did not stop the dialog from being saved. With an empty directory the plugin mounts named volumes instead of the chosen directory, while the adapter writes `config.yml` into the ioBroker data directory - Frigate then starts without its configuration\n- (@GermanBluefox) Removed the `iobBackup=frigate_data` label: no volume of that name exists, so it never marked anything. The label works for named volumes only, and everything worth keeping lives in the bind-mounted Frigate directory - `config.yml` is generated from the instance settings, which an ioBroker backup contains anyway, and recordings and clips are far too large for one","tree":{"sha":"1591eccdf969973707ee2714471f37e749865f73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/git/trees/1591eccdf969973707ee2714471f37e749865f73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/git/commits/a571109d94e05e00605d7ede3d00a176d02a0347","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ge