":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/commits/ed1f776b5d4c502c5d9bee465a302a8f375fd574/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T14:30:11Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T14:30:11Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v3.1.1\n\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed the clip download failing with `Request failed with status code 400`: Frigate answers that while the recording segments of the event are not written yet, so the download is now retried with a growing delay and the message Frigate sent is written to the log instead of only the status code. The default wait time after the event end was raised from 5 to 10 seconds\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added the missing translations for the LPR settings, the go2rtc restream column and the event history header, and corrected translations where the product name `Frigate`, state IDs and the `{{source}}`/`{{type}}` placeholders had been translated as words\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed stale `.jpg` / `.mp4` files in the tmp folder: the cleanup no longer depends on `notificationActive`, aborted downloads and failed notifications no longer leave files behind, and every instance now uses its own tmp folder (`iobroker-frigate.<instance>`)\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added a web extension: every camera is now served under `/frigate.0/<camera>/snapshot.jpg` and `/frigate.0/<camera>/stream.mjpeg` of the web adapter, behind the ioBroker authentication and without exposing Frigate itself\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added two widgets for ioBroker.devices: a snapshot tile that works everywhere, and a live MJPEG tile\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added the `snapshot` message, which returns the current picture of a camera as base64\n- (Eistee82) Fixed zone object counters (e.g. `<zone>.person`) staying at their last value after the object left the zone. Per-zone object counts are now sourced solely from the Frigate MQTT occupancy topics, and the zone aggregator resets its active/stationary states to 0 and uses `current_zones` instead of the cumulative `entered_zones`.","tree":{"sha":"b03df8a58ea9db523e1a64f0769de8282198d7d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/git/trees/b03df8a58ea9db523e1a64f0769de8282198d7d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/git/commits/ed1f776b5d4c502c5d9bee465a302a8f375fd574","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/commit/ed1f776b5d4c502c5d9bee465a302a8f375fd574","node_id":"C_kwDOLHy_BNoAKGVkMWY3NzZiNWQ0YzUwMmM1ZDliZWU0NjVhMzAyYThmMzc1ZmQ1NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/commit/a063fd62961c622ea76402c9ec55b02f2fd4ccc3","sha":"a063fd62961c622ea76402c9ec55b02f2fd4ccc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/commits/a063fd62961c622ea76402c9ec55b02f2fd4ccc3"}],"sha":"ed1f776b5d4c502c5d9bee465a302a8f375fd574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/commits/ed1f776b5d4c502c5d9bee465a302a8f375fd574"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/commits/a063fd62961c622ea76402c9ec55b02f2fd4ccc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:55:48Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:55:48Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"fix: retry the clip download and log the reason Frigate sends (#274)\n\nFrigate answers `/api/events/<id>/clip.mp4` with `400 No recordings found\nfor the specified time range` while the recording segments of the event are\nnot written to the disk yet. The adapter waited only 5 seconds after the\nevent end, made a single attempt and gave up, so clips were silently lost.\n\n- downloadStreamToFile returns a DownloadResult instead of a boolean and\n  reads the error body. With responseType ''stream'' axios puts the body into\n  a stream, so Frigate''s `{\"success\": false, \"message\": \"...\"}` was thrown\n  away and the log only showed \"Request failed with status code 400\".\n- New downloadClipWithRetry: up to 3 attempts with a doubling delay. Only\n  400, 5xx and \"no response at all\" are retried; a 404 (clip not available)\n  is not, because the clip will never appear.\n- Raised the default wait time after the event end from 5 to 10 seconds and\n  added a help text to the field in the admin, translated into all languages.\n- Added tests for the retry, for giving up, for the 404 case and for the\n  error message ending up in the log.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"852863e54f0759d89954c2d805d32effb3881cae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/git/trees/852863e54f0759d89954c2d805d32effb3881cae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.frigate/git/commits/a063fd62961c622ea76402c9ec55b02f2fd4ccc3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github